5,1,1,talk,Asuka,,We need to verify if previous initiatives actually worked before spending more. I will check the readmission figures and the shared nursing round data.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Toshio,,"I’m concerned about physical capacity. I’ll check rooms, parking, and shuttle coverage to see if we can absorb another program.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,"I suspect our failures stem from structural rot, not bad ideas. I’ll check the board minutes and the data agreements to see where the joints cracked.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Yumi,,I’m worried about who actually carries the new workload. I’ll check the ward nursing vacancies and the therapy staffing review to see where the pressure lands.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Servas,,I worry about the long-term cost. I will check the development allocation and the regional fund tariffs to see what we can truly afford.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Asuka,,"I want to ensure we don't repeat past mistakes. @Toshio, do you think physical space is the main bottleneck for any new program?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, space is critical, but the booking system is the real choke point. If it can’t log the work, it doesn’t exist.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, the booking system is a symptom, not the cause. The real fracture is when partners refuse to sign the data agreements.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, I hear you, but even with perfect data, if the nurses are already stretched thin, the program just collapses under the weight.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Servas,,"@Yumi, you are right. A program without sustainable funding is merely a temporary burden. We must ensure the money lasts beyond the initial excitement.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, structural rot is real, but I need proof of impact. Did the call-back trial actually reduce readmissions, or was it just noise?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, the trial’s success is irrelevant if the infrastructure cannot handle the volume. I am focused on whether the physical and digital systems can absorb the load.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, the trial worked, but the rot is in the maintenance. I’m checking the board minutes and data agreements to see where the joints cracked.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Asuka, the trial’s success is a start, but I need to know if the teams can sustain it. I’m checking the staffing records to see who is already at breaking point.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
